═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
💡 EDGE CASES & CONSIDERATIONS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DST Transitions:
- In spring: Lost hour (2:00am → 3:00am)
- In fall: Repeated hour (2:00am happens twice)
- Never schedule during transition times
- Use library functions (don't calculate manually!)

UTC Offsets:
- DON'T hardcode offsets (DST changes)
- DON'T use offsets like "UTC-5" (ambiguous)
- DO use IANA codes like "America/New_York" (correct)

Crossing Dateline:
- Customer in UTC+12 booking with team in UTC-11
- Same calendar day but 23 hours apart!
- Always use UTC internally for clarity

Displaying Time:
- Always include timezone abbreviation
- Show UTC as fallback
- Don't assume "am/pm" (other countries use 24h)

Mobile Considerations:
- Detect timezone from device
- Allow easy override
- Show timezone clearly (not hidden)
- Small screen: use abbreviations (EDT not Eastern)


